      "description": "Watch Bayern München vs Union Berlin highlights and goals from Bundesliga on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on September 20, 2026. The atmosphere at the Allianz Arena was electric on September 20, 2026, as Bayern München hosted Union Berlin in a pivotal Bundesliga clash. With 75,024 fans in attendance, the stage was set for a high-intensity battle under the lights, with both sides eager to secure a statement victory. Bayern Take Control Early From the opening whistle, Bayern München established their dominance, controlling 69% of the ball and pinning Union Berlin deep into their own half. The breakthrough arrived in the 18th minute when Jamal Musiala unleashed a powerful strike from outside the box, beating Frederik Roennow to the bottom corner following a precise pass from Alphonso Davies . The goal energized the home crowd and set the tone for a relentless attacking display. The pressure mounted as the first half progressed. In the 38th minute, Michael Olise was tripped inside the area by Tom Rothe , prompting the referee to point to the spot. Harry Kane stepped up and coolly dispatched the penalty into the right corner. Just before the interval, Olise turned from provider to scorer, firing a left-footed shot from distance into the net in the 43rd minute after being set up by Musiala . Olise Completes a Historic Hattrick The second half saw no let-up from the Bavarian giants. Harry Kane added his second of the match in the 54th minute, heading home a cross from Michael Olise . Despite multiple tactical substitutions from Union Berlin , including the introduction of Tim Skarke and Derrick Koehn , they struggled to contain the wave of attacks. Ismael Saibari , a second-half substitute himself, made an immediate impact by scoring the fifth goal in the 70th minute. The final stages of the match belonged entirely to Michael Olise . The Frenchman completed a spectacular hattrick with two quickfire goals in the 73rd and 76th minutes, both assisted by the impressive youngster Tom Bischof . As Olise left the field in the 77th minute to a standing ovation, he claimed the match ball as a souvenir of a masterclass performance that left the visitors searching for answers. The match concluded with Bayern firmly in command, having delivered one of the most dominant performances of the season."
